@startuml
title Sprint 2 - Current and Proposed Data Model
hide methods
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam packageStyle rectangle

legend right
  Existing Payload collections are inside "Current app".
  Sprint 2 additions for issue #4 are Cloud Firestore documents.
  Existing app users are referenced by their Payload string IDs.
endlegend

package "Current app" {
  class User {
    id: PayloadID
    email: string
    username: string
    name: string
    role: student | test | admin
  }

  class Course {
    id: PayloadID
    code: string {unique}
    name: string
    level: enum
    color: enum
  }

  class Task {
    id: PayloadID
    title: string
    classLevel: enum
    assignmentType: enum
    dueDate: datetime?
    plannedStart: datetime?
    estimatedMinutes: number
    status: open | scheduled | done
    score: number [computed]
    owner: User
    course: Course?
    calendarEvent: CalendarEvent?
  }

  class CalendarEvent {
    id: PayloadID
    title: string
    start: datetime
    end: datetime
    allDay: boolean
    completed: boolean
    kind: enum
    location: string?
    description: string?
    uid: string
    source: ics-file | ics-url | manual
    sourceKey: string? {indexed}
    owner: User
    course: Course?
  }
}

package "Sprint 2 - Cloud Firestore" {
  class TeamProject {
    id: string [document ID]
    title: string
    description: string?
    finalDeadline: Timestamp
    ownerId: string
    createdAt: Timestamp
    updatedAt: Timestamp
  }

  class ProjectMember {
    documentId: encoded userId
    userId: string
    name: string
    username: string
    role: owner | member
    createdAt: Timestamp
  }

  class Deliverable {
    id: string [document ID]
    projectId: string
    parentDeliverableId: string?
    assigneeId: string
    assigneeName: string
    assigneeUsername: string
    title: string
    description: string?
    dueAt: Timestamp
    status: open | in-progress | done
    createdAt: Timestamp
    updatedAt: Timestamp
  }

  class TeamUserDirectory {
    documentId: encoded userId
    userId: string
    name: string
    username: string
    nameNormalized: string
    usernameNormalized: string
    updatedAt: Timestamp
  }

  class UserProjectIndex {
    projectId: string
    role: owner | member
    createdAt: Timestamp
  }
}

User "1" <-- "0..*" Task : owns
Course "0..1" <-- "0..*" Task : for
CalendarEvent "0..1" <-- "0..*" Task : imported from
User "1" <-- "0..*" CalendarEvent : owns
Course "0..1" <-- "0..*" CalendarEvent : for

User "1" <-- "0..*" TeamProject : ownerId reference
TeamProject "1" <-- "1..*" ProjectMember : members subcollection
User "1" <-- "0..*" ProjectMember : userId reference
TeamProject "1" <-- "0..*" Deliverable : deliverables subcollection
Deliverable "0..1" <-- "0..*" Deliverable : parent / children
ProjectMember "1" <-- "0..*" Deliverable : assignee membership
User "1" <-- "1" TeamUserDirectory : userId reference
TeamUserDirectory "1" <-- "0..*" UserProjectIndex : projects subcollection
TeamProject "1" <-- "0..*" UserProjectIndex : projectId reference

note bottom of Deliverable
  Enforced invariants:
  - assignee must be a member of the project
  - parent and child belong to the same project
  - dueAt <= project.finalDeadline - 72 hours
end note

note right of ProjectMember
  Unique membership is enforced by using
  the encoded userId as the subcollection
  document ID.
end note

note right of TeamUserDirectory
  Contains only a user's name and username
  plus normalized search fields. No email
  or credentials are copied from Payload.
end note
@enduml
